    },
    "slide2_executive_summary": {
      "value": "LTIMindtree delivered ₹38,008 Cr consolidated revenue ($4,492M, +5.0% CC) in FY25 (+7.0% YoY in INR), with Operating Profit (EBITDA) of ₹6,495 Cr (17.1% margin) and Net Profit (PAT) of ₹4,602 Cr (EPS ₹155.47). Note: FY19–FY21 represent pre-merger standalone LTI while FY22–FY25 reflect the combined LTIMindtree entity.",
      "source": "LTM-Recalculated.xlsx!Income Statement"
    },
    "slide2_thesis": {
      "value": "Our connected 5-year FCFF DCF model projects USD constant-currency growth accelerating from 7.5% in FY26E to 8.5%–9.0% over FY27E–FY30E across realized USD/INR exchange rates of ₹85.50–₹87.50, driving INR revenue to ₹60,111 Cr by FY30E. Discounting explicit FCFF at an 11.50% CAPM WACC (Rf 7.30%, Beta 0.95, ERP 4.46%) with 5.00% terminal growth and adding ₹10,158 Cr net cash yields ₹83,336 Cr Equity Value or ₹2,813.51/share (vs ₹5,568.00 snapshot CMP).",
      "source": "LTM-Recalculated.xlsx!FCFF Valuation"
    },
    "slide2_key_highlights": {
      "value": "• FY25 Consolidated Revenue: ₹38,008 Cr ($4,492M, +5.0% CC); FY25 PAT: ₹4,602 Cr (EPS ₹155.47)\n• Merger Boundary: FY19–FY21 Pre-Merger LTI | FY22 Restated Combined | FY23–FY25 Merged LTIMindtree\n• Connected 5Y Forecast: USD CC growth (7.5%–9.0%) * FX (₹85.50–₹87.50) -> FY26E ₹41,288 Cr to FY30E ₹60,111 Cr\n• CAPM WACC Schedule: Ke 11.54% (99.3% weight) + Post-Tax Kd 5.96% (0.7% weight) = 11.50% WACC\n• Implied DCF Equity Value: ₹83,336 Cr (₹2,813.51 / share vs ₹5,568.00 15-Oct-2025 CMP)",
      "source": "LTM-Recalculated.xlsx!FCFF Valuation"
    },
